  "live_records": {
    "q-181129": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181129",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14191375/assets/d550ecec3b7103c9510b6e45e738ae1385e07fa63ff2e50c54da6c17606faaec.png)\n\nDescribe the set of points shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in \\{-3,-2,-1\\},\\,y\\in \\{-4,-3,-2,-1\\}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
