    "q-181678": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181678",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14191375/assets/0f95f6b259237816a5a3da041452cfd9458f0852b1ae717a044738b6f310ab5d.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,3\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2x+3\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=3$ and *below* the line $y=2x+3.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>3,\\,y<2x+3.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n3<y<2x+3.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=3$ and $y=2x+3$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\le y\\le 2x+3\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\le y\\le 2x+3\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "select",
          "dom_id": "selectList-181678-0",
          "tag": "custom-select",
